WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
OSHA 10 is not optional. You need this to work on most commercial job sites.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Personal protective equipment selection and use. Safety glasses for all HVAC
work. Gloves appropriate to the task: leather for handling sheet metal,
heat-resistant for brazing, chemical-resistant for refrigerant handling.

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
PPE: Personal Protective Equipment selected based on the specific hazards of
each task.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: PPE is not optional. Employers provide it
but you must wear it. Violations result in discipline or termination.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: Match PPE to the specific hazard. And — Safety glasses are
required for ALL HVAC work

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

